.TH ASTERCTL-SUBSCRIPTIONS 1 "2026-10-02" "Aster" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
asterctl-subscriptions \- list Event subscriptions
.SH SYNOPSIS
.SY asterctl
.RI [ GLOBAL-OPTIONS ]
.B subscriptions
.YS
.SH DESCRIPTION
List this node's Event subscriptions, ordered by subscription ID.
.SH OPTIONS
Accepts the global options described in
.BR asterctl (1).
.SH OUTPUT
Prints each subscription as a block with the following fields:
.TP
.B ID
Full Base64 subscription ID.
.TP
.B Topic
Subscribed topic.
.TP
.B Scope
Subscribed scope. A trailing '/*' includes sub-scopes.
.TP
.B Operation key
The key used to create the subscription. UTF-8 keys are quoted and escaped;
other keys are shown as Base64 under the label "Operation key (Base64)".
.PP
With \-\-json, prints an array of objects containing:
.PP
.nf
.RS
subscriptionId           Base64 string
topic                    String
scope                    String, without the '/*' suffix
includeDescendantScopes  Boolean
operationKey             Base64 string
.RE
.fi
.PP
Unlike standard output, operationKey is always Base64.
.PP
An empty list produces no text output, or [] with \-\-json.
.SH EXIT STATUS
.TP
.B 0
Success, including an empty list.
.TP
.B 1
Command failed.
.TP
.B 2
Invalid or missing arguments.
.SH EXAMPLES
List subscriptions:
.PP
.nf
.RS
asterctl \-\-token\-file ./client.token subscriptions
.RE
.fi
.PP
List subscriptions as JSON:
.PP
.nf
.RS
asterctl \-\-token\-file ./client.token subscriptions \-\-json
.RE
.fi
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR asterctl (1),
.BR asterctl-subscribe (1),
.BR asterctl-query (1)
